[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) is marked known: one issue, one fix queued. Read by tenant and by the way
each report came in, its reports are not one issue. They split into separate problems, and the queued
parser fix closes only one of them. Each problem now has its own ticket.

<Callout kind="warn">
Do not close #4471 when the parser fix ships. The <code>hint</code> and <code>one-day</code> reports
stay broken after it.
</Callout>

## What #4471 holds

<ProblemTable
  ticket={4471}
  issues={{
    parser: 'https://github.com/BNewman73/what-it-shows/issues/1',
    hint: 'https://github.com/BNewman73/what-it-shows/issues/2',
    'one-day': 'https://github.com/BNewman73/what-it-shows/issues/3',
  }}
/>

## The problems

**`parser`: the shared parser reads dates month first.** Every tenant on file writes the day first.
A booking on 7 April goes out on 4 July. This is the fix #4471 already has queued.
[Ticket](https://github.com/BNewman73/what-it-shows/issues/1).

**`hint`: the booking-v3 form tells people to type month first.** booking-v3 prints `MM/DD/YYYY`
under its date field, then reads the date in the tenant's order, day first. People type what the hint
says, so the date is swapped before the parser sees it. Only reports that came in through that form,
from tenants on booking-v3. The parser fix does not touch it.
[Ticket](https://github.com/BNewman73/what-it-shows/issues/2).

**`one-day`: bookings move by one day.** "Client in Lisbon got Tuesday. Client in Toronto got Monday.
Same meeting." No day and month are swapped here, so neither fix above closes these. It looks like a
time-zone or day-boundary problem. The desk had already read these reports as a one-day move
(`desk-notes.json`), but #4471's table counts them under `parser` because of their tenant.
[Ticket](https://github.com/BNewman73/what-it-shows/issues/3).

## How the reports were placed

- **One report per id.** The ticket export comes in overlapping pages, so some reports appear twice.
- **By tenant, not by intake tag.** Intake guesses a tag from the reporter's browser. The tenant's
  locale and booking form decide the cause (`src/lib/kb/causes.ts`). The two disagree often; the
  table shows how often.
- **One-day moves first.** A report the desk read as a one-day move is `one-day`, whatever its tenant
  (`src/lib/kb/problems.ts`).
- **Every body was read.** All other reports describe a day and month swapped, or say only that the
  date was wrong.

## Lessons

- A big ticket can be several bugs with the same symptom. Count by cause, not by subject.
- A footnote under a table is a finding nobody owns. Give it a ticket.

